{"availability":"available","full":"dguywhoknows/accessible-palette-generator","name":"accessible-palette-generator","description":"AI color palettes from a mood or brand, checked with real color science: OKLCH tonal scales, a WCAG contrast matrix, auto-fix, color-blindness simulation and a live UI preview.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-07T04:17:38Z","updated":"2026-10-10T03:50:52Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dguywhoknows.github.io/accessible-palette-generator/","topics":["accessibility","color","github-pages","javascript","oklch","wcag"],"demo":"https://dguywhoknows.github.io/accessible-palette-generator/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.300Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.300Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.300Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.300Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["AI color palettes from a mood or brand, checked with real color science: OKLCH tonal scales, a WCAG contrast matrix, auto-fix, color-blindness simulation and a live UI preview.","Describe a brand or mood and the AI designs a 7-role UI palette (primary, secondary, accent, background, surface, text, muted). Everything after that is local color science. Colors are converted to OKLCH (Björn Ottosson's OKLab) to build perceptually even 50–950 tonal scales with gamut mapping. A WCAG 2.x contrast matrix grades every foreground/background pair, and auto-fix nudges OKLCH lightness until text passes AA. Machado-2009 color-blindness simulation flags key colors that become indistinguishable. A live preview shows the palette on a mock dashboard in light and a derived dark mode.…"],"features":["AI palette design for 7 semantic roles, with names and rationale","Lock + regenerate: the AI harmonizes new colors around the ones you keep","OKLCH conversion, chroma-curved tonal scales (50-950) with binary-search gamut mapping","WCAG contrast matrix with AA/AAA/large badges; one-click auto-fix via lightness search","Color-vision simulation (protan, deutan, tritan, achromat) with ΔE-OK confusion warnings"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/accessible-palette-generator/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"56288ed0569c17b5044663f1424b276c3235a7eabc8a12e06149288cad99f8ec","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.391Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.391Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"AI color palettes from a mood or brand, checked with real color science: OKLCH tonal scales, a WCAG contrast matrix, auto-fix, color-blindness simulation and a live UI preview.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/accessible-palette-generator/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"index.html is the public home page, login.html handles accounts and app.html is the app.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/accessible-palette-generator/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"56288ed0569c17b5044663f1424b276c3235a7eabc8a12e06149288cad99f8ec","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/accessible-palette-generator/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.391Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-10T03:50:52Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dguywhoknows/accessible-palette-generator/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.392Z","hash":"56288ed0569c17b5044663f1424b276c3235a7eabc8a12e06149288cad99f8ec","originalBytes":5574,"storedBytes":5574,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["contrast","page","src","app","color","colors","every","lib","live","oklch","tests","wcag","browser","settings","simulation","design","image","lightness","palette","runs","scales","text","accounts","auto-fix","background","brand","build","core.js","css","dark","exports","functions","generated","harmony","index.html","key","matrix","mode",